				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/name" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(254716); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=254716&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607850063" alt="name" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=254716)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/name" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(254716); return false;" >name</a></span> <span class="odate time_1237233977 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">16 Mar 2009 20:06</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-418477">
									

<p>Its a clever and inventive idea- an army of ables, with all his ability but non of the sociopathy. We would only turn people into him that we knew were 100 percent loyal, and we could control them the same way we control the original; with an explosive collar just in case. Yes, he probably would freak out and try to kill them all if he knew, but who's to say he has to be told? And think, we can flay him all we want, but eventually he'll just regenerate, so the number of troops is limitless. Hey! Maybe that's why the guy tried to infiltrate the site! To steal skin. Makes sense.</p>
<p>Of course, going behind his back like that would be dangerous, but definitely interesting. I can imagine The Foundation keeping that secret from him, covering it up, hiding the different versions when he walks by.</p>
<p>Maybe they have a couple strips of skin stocked up just in case he goes completely rogue and somehow escapes?</p>
<p>This kind of ties into an idea i was thinking about. We're given the perception that the Foundation is extremely powerful, especially by the implication that they successfully capture all these keter class objects and foil their escape attempts. Like 682 for example; it's not really said exactly how it's stopped every time, but they do it. How? The Foundation doesn't have access to super science, so what sets them apart from normal soldiers and commandos? Obviously they use SCPs to their fullest advantage. I think this would be one of them.</p>
<p>Two things though Lacynt:</p>
<p>It couldn't be used on 682, it doesn't work on animals. On that line of thought, maybe it wouldn't work of able either; i mean he's not exactly human is he? didn't the article say something about his organs being different.<br />
Secondly, not every object has to have a use or be destroyed. Thats a really bad misconception. The Foundation contains almost everything, even if it costs money or has no purpose. That's its job. If it was all about the benefits it wouldn't need funding. But its not a business or something thats completely self-sufficient. I bet governments pump money into this organization. So it doesn't have to do anything helpful. It just has to be special. I really dislike the other point of view.</p>

							</div>

								
					
