														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-651303">
									

<p>Except for name who directly mentions this in his post.<br />
Is Able classified as non-human? Just because he is ever-respawning doesn't necessarily make it so that he is non-human. Although it is a good indication. The series canon with the interaction of Cain and Able in the Wanderlust points to emotions similar to what would come from the Bible story of the two brothers of the first human family.<br />
Anyway, the testing of such an experiment would be tricky, as it would have to be an unquestioningly loyal Agent or Doctor to not abuse the powers granted to him. Also, if we killed Able while someone was disguised as him, would the disguise fade because Able isn't technically dead, just not entirely alive? Another consideration, if the 'death' of Able ends the disguise, will his reincarnation restart it if the time hasn't expired? What about samples of flesh harvested from Ables that have 'died' before?<br />
However, with the assertion that 034 "ONLY WORKS ON HUMANS" is contradicted quickly by saying "the results were… well… unexpected" meaning that 034 does work, just not in a manner that the Foundation likes. Further clarification should be done in the form of releasing of test files of animal/non-human species, or trying more experiments, preferably weaker easily controlled species selected.<br />
Does the limitation of 034 apply opposite the above proposition, with animals being tried to change into others of the same species and different species, before attempting making an animal into a human form.</p>
<p>If the author wants to work with me, I believe it might be fun creating an experimentation log with 034. Or perhaps with his blessing I can just create one.</p>

